# Template author: tinted-dircolors (local), modelled on seebi/dircolors-solarized
#
# Colors are 24-bit truecolor (38;2;R;G;B / 48;2;R;G;B) taken from the scheme,
# so they do not depend on the terminal's 16/256-color palette.
#
# Usage: eval "$(dircolors -b this-file)"

# Terminals that get colors at all
COLORTERM ?*
TERM Eterm
TERM ansi
TERM *color*
TERM con[0-9]*x[0-9]*
TERM cons25
TERM console
TERM cygwin
TERM *direct*
TERM dtterm
TERM gnome
TERM hurd
TERM jfbterm
TERM konsole
TERM kterm
TERM linux
TERM linux-c
TERM mlterm
TERM putty
TERM rxvt*
TERM screen*
TERM st
TERM terminator
TERM tmux*
TERM vt100
TERM vt220
TERM xterm*

## Basic file attributes
RESET 0
NORMAL 00
FILE 00
DIR 01;38;2;@BLUE@
LINK 38;2;@CYAN@
MULTIHARDLINK 00
FIFO 38;2;@YELLOW@;48;2;@BG_ALT@
SOCK 01;38;2;@MAGENTA@
DOOR 01;38;2;@MAGENTA@
BLK 01;38;2;@YELLOW@;48;2;@BG_ALT@
CHR 01;38;2;@YELLOW@;48;2;@BG_ALT@
ORPHAN 01;38;2;@RED@;48;2;@BG_ALT@
MISSING 01;38;2;@RED@;48;2;@BG_ALT@
SETUID 38;2;@BG@;48;2;@RED@
SETGID 38;2;@BG@;48;2;@YELLOW@
CAPABILITY 38;2;@RED@;48;2;@BG_ALT@
STICKY_OTHER_WRITABLE 38;2;@BG@;48;2;@GREEN@
OTHER_WRITABLE 01;38;2;@BLUE@;48;2;@BG_ALT@
STICKY 38;2;@BG@;48;2;@BLUE@
EXEC 01;38;2;@GREEN@

